IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc17-dna-orders`

-- ccc17-tests-dna-orders.l4 -- tests for ccc17-dna-orders.l4 (ss 487.05 to 487.0552). Expected values are written from the text, beside each assertion;
-- JUST TRUE = the text brings the case within the provision; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered.

§ `Tests: s 487.05(1) the warrant`

-- all limbs met, in each of the four places of limb (b): JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(ii) on or within the body of the victim of the offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(iii) on anything worn or carried by the victim at the time when the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(iv) on or within the body of any person or thing or at any place associated with the commission of the offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- any one limb missing: NOTHING (a grant limited by its own wording)
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE NOTHING TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b) somewhere else` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests: s 487.05(2) criteria, s 487.05(4) execution in Canada`

#ASSERT `s 487.05(2) the provincial court judge shall have regard to the matter` `s 487.05(2)(a) the nature of the designated offence and the circumstances of its commission` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(2) the provincial court judge shall have regard to the matter` `s 487.05(2)(b)(i) whether there is a peace officer who is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take samples of bodily substances from the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(2) the provincial court judge shall have regard to the matter` `s 487.05(2)(b)(ii) whether there is another person who is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take samples under the direction of a peace officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(2) the provincial court judge shall have regard to the matter` `s 487.05(2) another matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(2) the provincial court judge shall have regard to the matter` `s 487.05(2) another matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.05(4) the warrant may be executed by the peace officer at the place` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(4) the warrant may be executed by the peace officer at the place` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.05(4) the warrant may be executed by the peace officer at the place` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests: s 487.051 orders`

-- (1): each of the four ways the person stands, with a primary designated offence within (a) or (c.02)
#ASSERT `s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 convicted` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 discharged under section 730` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 found guilty under the Young Offenders Act` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 convicted` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 convicted` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 none of those` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the person must establish gross disproportion; the court is then "not required to make the order"
#ASSERT `s 487.051(2) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 convicted` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(2) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 discharged under section 730` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(2) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 convicted` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(2) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 convicted` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(2) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 convicted` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(2) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(2) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` `s 487.051 none of those` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): application by the prosecutor + best interests + (a) not criminally responsible with a designated offence, or (b) convicted etc. with a secondary designated offence
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE TRUE `s 487.051 found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE TRUE `s 487.051 convicted` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE TRUE `s 487.051 discharged under section 730` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE TRUE `s 487.051 found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE TRUE `s 487.051 found guilty under the Young Offenders Act` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` FALSE TRUE `s 487.051 convicted` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE FALSE `s 487.051 convicted` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE TRUE `s 487.051 convicted` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE TRUE `s 487.051 found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` TRUE TRUE `s 487.051 none of those` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) closing words: the matters, reasons
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court shall consider the matter in deciding whether to make the order` `s 487.051(3) the person’s criminal record` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court shall consider the matter in deciding whether to make the order` `s 487.051(3) whether they were previously found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court shall consider the matter in deciding whether to make the order` `s 487.051(3) the nature of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court shall consider the matter in deciding whether to make the order` `s 487.051(3) the circumstances surrounding its commission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court shall consider the matter in deciding whether to make the order` `s 487.051(3) the impact such an order would have on the person’s privacy and security of the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court shall consider the matter in deciding whether to make the order` `s 487.051(3) another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(3) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): "When the court makes an order authorizing the taking" (group G1: JUST FALSE when the "when" fails)
#ASSERT `s 487.051(4) the court may make an order in Form 5.041 requiring the person to report and submit to the taking of the samples` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.051(4) the court may make an order in Form 5.041 requiring the person to report and submit to the taking of the samples` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests: s 487.053 timing and hearing`

#ASSERT `s 487.053(1) the court may make an order under section 487.051 at this time` `s 487.053(1) it imposes a sentence on a person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(1) the court may make an order under section 487.051 at this time` `s 487.053(1) it finds the person not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(1) the court may make an order under section 487.051 at this time` `s 487.053(1) it directs that they be discharged under section 730` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(1) the court may make an order under section 487.051 at this time` `s 487.053(1) another occasion` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(a) the court shall set a date for a hearing within 90 days` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(a) the court shall set a date for a hearing within 90 days` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(b) the court retains jurisdiction over the matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(b) the court retains jurisdiction over the matter` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(c) the court may require the person to appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(c) the court may require the person to appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(c) the court may require the person to appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the 90 days: sentence on 1 January 2026; January has 31 days, February 28, March 31: day 90 is 1 April 2026
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(a) the last day for the court to set a date for the hearing` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(a) the court set the date within 90 days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(a) the court set the date within 90 days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.053(2)(a) the court set the date within 90 days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
-- the same duty as a regulative rule: the court MUST set the date WITHIN 90 (days after the sentence, finding or discharge). A #TRACE is read, not asserted (the stable binary
-- cannot compare a DEONTIC value with EQUALS): the first trace, on day 90, ends FULFILLED; the second, on day 91, ends in a BREACH BY `the court`.
#TRACE `s 487.053(2)(a) the court must set a date for the hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 487.053(2)(a) set a date for a hearing` AT 90
#TRACE `s 487.053(2)(a) the court must set a date for the hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 487.053(2)(a) set a date for a hearing` AT 91

§ `Tests: s 487.054 appeal`

#ASSERT `s 487.054 the person may appeal from the decision of the court` `s 487.054 the offender` `s 487.054 a decision under subsection 487.051(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.054 the person may appeal from the decision of the court` `s 487.054 the offender` `s 487.054 a decision under subsection 487.051(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.054 the person may appeal from the decision of the court` `s 487.054 the prosecutor` `s 487.054 a decision under subsection 487.051(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.054 the person may appeal from the decision of the court` `s 487.054 someone else` `s 487.054 a decision under subsection 487.051(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.054 the person may appeal from the decision of the court` `s 487.054 the offender` `s 487.054 another decision` EQUALS NOTHING

